// Title: Suspicious Scheduled Task Write to System32 Tasks
// Sigma ID: 80e1f67a-4596-4351-98f5-a9c3efabac95
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-11-16 | Modified: 2022-01-12
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, T1053
// Description: Detects the creation of tasks from processes executed from suspicious locations
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_task_write.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks" and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\AppData\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "C:\\PerfLogs" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\Windows\\System32\\config\\systemprofile")
